{{also|Cote d'Ivoire}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fr|en}} ''[[côte]]'' + ''{{l|fr|de|d'}}'' + ''[[ivoire]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌkəʊt diːˈvwɑː/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-Côte d'Ivoire.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The [[Ivory Coast]].

====Usage notes====
* The country has been known in [[English]] as ''Ivory Coast'', and corresponding translations in other languages. In October 1985 the government requested that the country be known as Côte d'Ivoire in every language. Read more at [[w:Côte d'Ivoire#Names|Wikipedia]].

